.TH FERMI_SSO_SITES 5 "2026-10-30" "requests-fermi-sso 0.4.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
fermi_sso_sites \- catalog of SSO\-protected sites for the fermi\-sso\-jar tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.fermi_sso/sites.yaml
.br
.B $FERMI_SSO_SITES_FILE
.br
.I config/sites.yaml
(reference copy of the built\-in catalog)
.SH DESCRIPTION
A
.I site
is the handful of facts
.BR fermi_sso_jar (1)
and its viewers need to sign in to one service provider and to tell
afterwards whether the jar still carries its session. The catalog is
built by merging, in order:
.IP 1. 4
the built\-in entries (Mu2e DocDB, the Mu2e shift scheduler, Mu2eTalks,
SCD Reporting, Fermilab ServiceNow), identical to
.IR config/sites.yaml ;
.IP 2. 4
.IR ~/.fermi_sso/sites.yaml ,
the user catalog that
.B fermi_sso_jar sites add
writes;
.IP 3. 4
the files named in
.BR $FERMI_SSO_SITES_FILE ,
colon separated (semicolon on Windows);
.IP 4. 4
any
.BI "\-\-sites\-file " FILE
options.
.PP
A later file overrides an earlier entry with the same key field by field,
so a user file may change only
.B expect
for a built\-in site and keep the rest. An entry of
.B enabled: false
(or a null entry) hides a site; a still later file may re\-enable it.
Missing files from steps 2 and 3 are skipped; a missing
.B \-\-sites\-file
is an error.
.PP
Files are YAML and need PyYAML. A file whose first character is
.B {
is read as JSON with the standard library instead.
.SH FORMAT
.EX
settings:                       # optional, all keys optional
  cookie_file: ~/.fermi_sso.cookies
  margin: 1800                  # seconds; sooner expiry counts as stale
  idp_host: pingprod.fnal.gov
  user: myaccount
  auth: password                # password | kerberos | yubikey
  pin_source: ~/.fermi_sso.pin

sites:
  KEY:
    name: Human label           # default: the key
    url: https://host/sso/entry # required; https only
    expect: Dashboard           # text required on the signed-in page
    domains: [host.fnal.gov]    # cookie domains of the site session;
                                # default: the host of url. Subdomains match.
    connection: oidc            # saml | oidc; default unknown
    auth: [password, kerberos]  # methods known to work; default all
    js_redirect: false          # follow a JavaScript location= stub
    notes: free text
    enabled: true
.EE
.PP
.I KEY
is lowercase letters, digits, dots, underscores and dashes, starting with
a letter or digit. Unknown fields are rejected, so a typo cannot silently
disable a check.
.PP
The
.B settings
block sits between the env file and the built\-in defaults in the tools'
precedence order: commandline, environment, env file, settings, defaults.
.SS Choosing the url
Use the URL that starts the login, not the site root. Site roots are
usually unprotected landing pages (DocDB) or local login menus (the shift
scheduler, allauth applications), and a login that never happens cannot
be verified. Known shapes:
.TP
DocDB (SAML)
.I https://mu2e\-docdb.fnal.gov/cgi\-bin/sso/DocumentDatabase
.TP
Flask/OIDC applications
.I https://mu2e\-shifts.fnal.gov/login/oidc?next=/
.TP
django\-allauth applications
.I https://mu2e\-talks.fnal.gov/accounts/oidc/keycloak/login/?next=%2F
.TP
ServiceNow
.I https://fermi.servicenowservices.com/navpage.do
with
.BR "js_redirect: true" ,
because protected pages answer with a page whose only content is a
JavaScript jump to the identity provider.
.SS connection
PingFederate runs two connections that do not share a login. Sites on the
same connection share one identity\-provider session in the jar: priming
any one of them signs the rest in through a bare redirect chain. The
value is informational for the tools today and is shown in the status
table so that the first login per connection is predictable.
.SS auth
The SAML connection does not offer the YubiKey adapter, so DocDB and
ServiceNow list
.BR "[password, kerberos]" .
The tools do not refuse a method that is not listed; the list documents
what has been seen to work.
.SH EXAMPLES
A user file that adds a site and narrows a built\-in one:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sites:
  my\-app:
    url: https://my\-app.fnal.gov/login/oidc?next=/
    expect: Dashboard
    connection: oidc
  servicenow:
    enabled: false
.EE
.RE
.PP
The same written by the tool:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fermi_sso_jar sites add my\-app "https://my\-app.fnal.gov/login/oidc?next=/" \-x Dashboard \-\-connection oidc
fermi_sso_jar sites remove servicenow
.EE
.RE
.PP
A project catalog used alongside the user one:
.PP
.RS
.EX
export FERMI_SSO_SITES_FILE=~/project/config/sso\-sites.yaml
fermi_sso_jar sites list
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.fermi_sso/sites.yaml
User catalog, mode 600, directory mode 700.
.TP
.I config/sites.yaml
In the source tree and installed under
.IR share/fermi\-sso/config/ :
the built\-in catalog with every field commented.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fermi_sso_jar (1),
.BR fermi_sso_jar_tui (1),
.BR fermi_sso_jar_gui (1),
.BR fermi_sso_probe (1)
